            <ArticleTitle>Fistula between a branch of left anterior descending coronary artery and pulmonary artery with spontaneous closure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>954-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Communication between a branch of left anterior descending coronary artery and main pulmonary artery is rare and has been previously described. However, spontaneous closure has not been described previously. We report such a case in a 41-year-old man with exertional angina and coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
